{"schema":1,"slug":"ojibwe-and-odawa-on-birds-war-road","nation":"Ojibwe (Chippewa) and Odawa","baseRef":"/data/web/territories/_base-great-lakes.json","yearStart":1780,"yearEnd":1780,"presenceLabel":"Ojibwe and Odawa war road, June 1780","presenceNote":"Event route: one campaign (25 May–4 Aug 1780; in Kentucky 21–25 June). The area is an approximate general area of Odawa and Ojibwe presence c.1700–1819 (Sault Ste. Marie, the Straits, Detroit, Saginaw and the Maumee; from 1807 and 1819 also the Saginaw and Thunder Bay counties named in the treaties). The wider homeland (Wisconsin, Minnesota, Ontario) is text only and is not drawn. The Odawa also have their own story, Egushawa and the Odawa in Kentucky’s War Years, which is a separate page and is not merged here.","confidence":"low-medium","approximate":true,"overlapNote":"The route followed the Great Miami through Shawnee country and the Licking through the northern Kentucky hunting grounds (Henderson). Bird’s force also had Delaware, Wyandot and Shawnee (ExploreKYHistory lists Delaware, Shawnee, Ottawa, Chippewa and Huron).","basis":"Wikipedia (Bird's invasion of Kentucky) for the route and the ~100 Odawa and Ojibwe, ExploreKYHistory #591, Greenville Art. 3 for Loramie's store. Route drawn on base-map river centrelines.","basisChip":"ethnohistory","timeline":{"min":1700,"max":1820},"fadeYears":0,"fadeSouth":false,"view":{"full":"158 0 540 679","narrow":"158 0 540 679","card":"158 0 540 679"},"mapLabelPos":[-83.9,44.3],"pins":[],"startEra":{"ojibwe-on-birds-war-road":"bird"},"stories":{"ojibwe-on-birds-war-road":{"yearStart":1780,"yearEnd":1780,"presenceLabel":"Ojibwe and Odawa war road"}},"legend":[{"kind":"soft","label":"Approximate general area of Odawa and Ojibwe presence (whole counties, not a boundary)"},{"kind":"line","label":"Licking River reach to Falmouth (solid, in Kentucky)"},{"kind":"point","label":"Site (exact position)"},{"kind":"ring","label":"Site, location approximate"}],"eras":[{"id":"home","label":"c.1700–1779 · Sault Ste. Marie, the Straits and Detroit","short":"c.1700","yearStart":1700,"yearEnd":1779,"confidence":"low-medium","sources":["ci_3f","wp_odawa","wp_ojibwe"],"storySlugs":[],"text":"The Three Fires (Ojibwe, Odawa and Potawatomi) held parts of Michigan, Wisconsin, Minnesota, Manitoba and Ontario (Canadian Encyclopedia). The Ojibwe were at Bawating (Sault Ste. Marie) and along Lake Superior; the Odawa ran from Michilimackinac to Manitoulin Island. Odawa and Ojibwe also lived in the Detroit, Maumee and Saginaw country. The tint is an approximate general area of the Michigan and Ohio part of that country, built from whole counties (Chippewa and Mackinac in the north; Detroit, Saginaw and the Maumee in the south). Wisconsin, Minnesota and Ontario are text only; the wider homeland is larger than this map shows. The c.1700 start is a round number.","layers":[{"feature":"oo_early","style":"soft"},{"feature":"sault","style":"point"},{"feature":"straits","style":"point"},{"feature":"detroit","style":"point"}],"apprTag":"Approximate general area · wider homeland not drawn","mapLabel":"OJIBWE · ODAWA","mapSubLabel":"approximate general area · c.1700–1779","mapLabelPos":[-84.3,44.4]},{"id":"bird","label":"25 May–Aug 1780 · Bird’s war road","short":"1780","yearStart":1780,"yearEnd":1780,"confidence":"low-medium","sources":["wp_bird","ekh591","greenville"],"storySlugs":["ojibwe-on-birds-war-road"],"text":"Bird left Detroit on 25 May 1780 with about 100 Odawa and Ojibwe from the tinted country (approximate general area), went up the Maumee and Auglaize, portaged to the Great Miami and down to the Ohio, joined McKee’s mostly Shawnee warriors, then went up the Licking and took Ruddle’s (22 June) and Martin’s Stations. Only the Kentucky reach (Ohio mouth to Falmouth) is drawn, as a solid line. The Odawa chief Egushawa has a separate story; it is not merged into this page.","layers":[{"feature":"oo_area","style":"soft"},{"feature":"licking_reach","style":"line"},{"feature":"detroit","style":"point"},{"feature":"martins","style":"point"}],"mapLabel":"OJIBWE · ODAWA","apprTag":"Approximate general area · route solid in Kentucky","mapSubLabel":"approximate general area · 1780 (came from here)","mapLabelPos":[-83.9,44.3]},{"id":"between","label":"1781–1806 · Michigan and the Maumee","short":"1781","yearStart":1781,"yearEnd":1806,"confidence":"low-medium","sources":["greenville","wp_odawa","wp_ojibwe"],"storySlugs":[],"text":"The same approximate general area carries on. Odawa and Ojibwe were among the nations that signed the Treaty of Greenville on 3 Aug 1795 (Avalon Project). The tint is built from whole counties and is not a boundary.","layers":[{"feature":"oo_early","style":"soft"},{"feature":"sault","style":"point"},{"feature":"straits","style":"point"},{"feature":"detroit","style":"point"}],"apprTag":"Approximate general area · wider homeland not drawn","mapLabel":"OJIBWE · ODAWA","mapSubLabel":"approximate general area · 1781–1806","mapLabelPos":[-84.3,44.4]},{"id":"treaties","label":"1807–1819 · Saginaw and Thunder Bay treaties","short":"1807","yearStart":1807,"yearEnd":1819,"confidence":"low-medium","sources":["tr1807","tr1819","ci_3f"],"storySlugs":[],"text":"The Treaty of Detroit (1807) ceded southeast Michigan and northwest Ohio and names a Chippewa blacksmith at Saginaw. The Treaty of Saginaw (1819) ceded land running to the head of the Thunder Bay River and reserved tracts on the Au Sable, Flint, Shiawassee, Tittabawassee and Saginaw rivers and elsewhere. The tint adds the counties those treaties name (Saginaw, Bay, Genesee, Shiawassee, Midland, Iosco and Alpena) to the earlier area. It is an approximate general area built from whole counties, not a treaty boundary.","layers":[{"feature":"oo_late","style":"soft"},{"feature":"sault","style":"point"},{"feature":"straits","style":"point"},{"feature":"detroit","style":"point"}],"apprTag":"Approximate general area · treaty counties added","mapLabel":"OJIBWE · ODAWA","mapSubLabel":"approximate general area · 1807–1819","mapLabelPos":[-84.3,44.4]}],"sources":[{"id":"wp_bird","label":"Bird's invasion of Kentucky (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bird%27s_invasion_of_Kentucky"},{"id":"ekh591","label":"British, Indian Raid (ExploreKYHistory #591)","url":"https://explorekyhistory.ky.gov/items/show/591"},{"id":"greenville","label":"Treaty of Greenville, 3 Aug 1795 (Avalon Project)","url":"https://avalon.law.yale.edu/18th_century/greenvil.asp"},{"id":"wp_odawa","label":"Odawa (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odawa"},{"id":"wp_ojibwe","label":"Ojibwe (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ojibwe"},{"id":"ci_3f","label":"Council of Three Fires (The Canadian Encyclopedia)","url":"https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/council-of-three-fires"},{"id":"tr1807","label":"Treaty with the Ottawa, etc., 1807 (Oklahoma State University treaty library)","url":"https://treaties.okstate.edu/treaties/treaty-with-the-ottawa-etc-1807-0092"},{"id":"tr1819","label":"Treaty with the Chippewa, 1819 (Oklahoma State University treaty library)","url":"https://treaties.okstate.edu/treaties/treaty-with-the-chippewa-1819-0185"}],"mainMap":{"general":"mm_general","lines":"mm_lines","points":"mm_points","labels":[{"text":"Ojibwe and Odawa: approximate general area c.1700–1819 (Sault Ste. Marie, the Straits, Detroit, Saginaw, Maumee); Bird’s 1780 route solid in Kentucky. Low–medium confidence","at":[-84.4,43.4]}]},"geojson":{"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"type":"Feature","properties":{"id":"detroit","note":"Detroit (Wikipedia 42.3317, -83.0459): Bird left on 25 May 1780 with 150 regulars and militia and roughly 100 Odawa and Ojibwe, two guns (Wikipedia, Bird's invasion).","approximate":true,"label":"Detroit","dx":9,"dy":5,"anchor":"start","name":"Detroit"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.0459,42.3317]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"id":"martins","note":"Martin's Station, Bourbon Co. (marker position 38.2626, -84.2938) and Ruddle's Station (no sourced coordinate); both surrendered 22-25 June 1780. Ruddle's attack is dated 21-22 June (Wikipedia).","approximate":true,"label":"Martin’s Station (1780, event)","dx":-9,"dy":-5,"anchor":"end","name":"Martin’s Station (1780, event)"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.2938,38.2626]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"id":"licking_reach","kind":"route (Kentucky reach)","note":"Licking River from its mouth to Falmouth (ExploreKYHistory: Byrd took the Licking to Falmouth, then overland to Ruddle's). Base-map Licking centreline. The overland leg to Ruddle's is NOT drawn (no sourced coordinates)."},"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-84.3272,38.6779],[-84.3239,38.7077],[-84.3174,38.7205],[-84.3315,38.7469],[-84.3466,38.769],[-84.3758,38.792],[-84.3876,38.809],[-84.4287,38.8192],[-84.4578,38.8447],[-84.4481,38.8754],[-84.4449,38.9162],[-84.4557,38.9494],[-84.433,38.9681],[-84.4406,38.9809],[-84.46,38.9698],[-84.4622,39.0013],[-84.4892,39.0269],[-84.4956,39.0635],[-84.5151,39.0873]]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"id":"extent","kind":"main-map extent","approximate":true,"note":"Main-map extent: general areas (whole-county shapes, approximate), solid lines in Kentucky and sourced points."},"geometry":{"type":"GeometryCollection","geometries":[{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[-84.8061,41.6961],[-84.3627,41.7091],[-84.3633,42.0735],[-84.1333,42.0752],[-84.1311,42.4246],[-83.6654,42.4379],[-83.6889,42.781],[-84.3637,42.7758],[-84.3706,43.4611],[-84.6075,43.466],[-84.606,43.8152],[-84.1728,43.8261],[-84.1664,43.9969],[-84.0454,43.997],[-84.0414,43.9124],[-83.9111,43.9105],[-83.9264,43.7873],[-83.9545,43.7559],[-83.9095,43.6732],[-83.6698,43.5915],[-83.5402,43.7087],[-83.4705,43.7236],[-83.4076,43.832],[-83.3346,43.8795],[-83.3474,43.9122],[-83.2832,43.9377],[-83.2615,43.9735],[-83.0669,44.0033],[-83.0246,44.0452],[-82.9161,44.0705],[-82.7462,43.996],[-82.6336,43.8312],[-82.598,43.5905],[-82.5